    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d287">

                <pb facs="0688" n="574" xml:id="pg574"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/8–943</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Halifax</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">most secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-09">August 9th,
                        1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Hull</hi>, On returning to the
                        Embassy<anchor n="1" xml:id="d287-f1"/> I found that three further telegrams
                    had come in on the subject of Italian surrender. I enclose copies, and will be
                    grateful if you could inform the President as soon as possible.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d287-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Yours very sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Halifax</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>





                <xi:include href="d287-a1.xml" xpointer="d287-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d287-a2.xml" xpointer="d287-a2"/>
                <xi:include href="d287-a3.xml" xpointer="d287-a3"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d287-f1" n="1" xml:id="d287-f1-content">
                <p>No record has been found of a conversation between Hull and Halifax on August 9,
                    1943, concerning Italy.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d287-f2" n="2" xml:id="d287-f2-content">
                <p>Hull showed the enclosures to Roosevelt on either August 9 or August 10. Attached
                    to copies of the enclosures in the Roosevelt Papers is the following memorandum
                    from George W. Renchard of Hull’s office to Roosevelt’s secretary (Tully):
                    “Although I believe the President read the attached messages during the
                    Secretary’s call on him the other day, I am sending them to you in the event you
                    wish to retain them in your files for future reference.” (Roosevelt Papers)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
